: "ZView desktop start-up.  An ordinary /bin/sh script, run by the window"
: "server when it comes up.  (The : lines predate the V3.4.5 sh, which does"
: "have # comments.)"
:
: "Since the PLACEHOLDER icons this script starts NOTHING by default: the"
: "start-up icon row is drawn by the server itself from /usr/hr/etc/apps"
: "(the icon and X,Y fields there), and an app is only launched -- and only"
: "then takes memory -- when its icon is clicked.  Closing its window frees"
: "that memory and puts the placeholder back."
:
: "Put a line here only for an app that must be genuinely RESIDENT from"
: "power-on, started in the BACKGROUND with & -- a GUI app does not exit"
: "while its window is open, so a line without & would hold this script,"
: "and the rest of the desktop, until that one window closed."
:
: "Options every GUI app understands (inc/hrapp.h):"
: "	-P <X>,<Y>	where to put the window (top-left of the frame)"
: "	-S <W>x<H>	content size, for a resizable app only"
: "	-T <title>	window title	-I <file.icn>	desktop icon"
: "	-H		start minimised to a desktop icon"
